description:
Develop a read-only memory (ROM) module that outputs a 16-bit data word based on an 8-bit address input. This design initializes the ROM with predefined binary values for addresses ranging from 0 to 15. The module utilizes an array to store the data and provides the corresponding data output based on the input address, effectively functioning as a look-up table where each address corresponds to a specific stored data value. The ROM can be classified as a mask ROM type due to the nature of its initialization.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] addr,
  output [m-1:0] data
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] addr,
  output [m-1:0] data
);parameter n = 8; // number of address signals
parameter m = 16; // number of data signals
parameter l = 8; // number of bits in each data word
parameter t = "mask ROM"; // type of ROM (mask ROM, programmable ROM, EPROM, EEPROM, or Flash)

// Define the data stored in the ROM as a set of binary values
reg [l-1:0] rom [2**n-1:0];

initial begin
  // Initialize the ROM with some data
  rom[0] = 8'b00000000;
  rom[1] = 8'b00000001;
  rom[2] = 8'b00000010;
  rom[3] = 8'b00000011;
  rom[4] = 8'b00000100;
  rom[5] = 8'b00000101;
  rom[6] = 8'b00000110;
  rom[7] = 8'b00000111;
  rom[8] = 8'b00001000;
  rom[9] = 8'b00001001;
  rom[10] = 8'b00001010;
  rom[11] = 8'b00001011;
  rom[12] = 8'b00001100;
  rom[13] = 8'b00001101;
  rom[14] = 8'b00001110;
  rom[15] = 8'b00001111;
end

// Connect the address signals to the data signals
assign data = rom[addr];

endmodule

